From fd7743475fa3a74b411a509274a567dd8bbc71ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Min Qin <qinmin@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:15:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/32] Preserve initiator StoragePartition for intercepted
 downloads

DownloadManagerImpl::InterceptNavigation() invokes
InterceptNavigationOnChecksComplete() via the embedder's asynchronous
CheckDownloadAllowed() callback and previously re-resolved the
initiating FrameTreeNode by ID. If the initiating subframe was detached
during this callback, the lookup returned null and the
StoragePartitionConfig fell back to the default partition, binding the
download's URLLoaderFactory and persisted embedder download data to the
incorrect partition.

Capture the initiator's StoragePartitionConfig synchronously in
InterceptNavigation() while the FrameTreeNode is active, and pass it
through the bound callback, matching the pattern used in
BeginResourceDownloadOnChecksComplete(). The post-callback
FrameTreeNode lookup is retained only for best-effort tab and frame
metadata.

Bug: 511803678
